1. वट् (prob. invented to serve as a root for the words below; cf. √ 1. वृत्) cl. 1. P., वटति (pf. ववाट &c.),
to surround, encompass, Dhātup. ix, 13;
 cl. 10. P. वटयति, to tie, string, connect, xxxv, 5;
to divide, partition, xxxv, 65;
to speak, xix, 17:
Pass. वट्यते (only वट्यन्ते, Viṣṇ. xliii, 34), to be crushed or pounded or ground down.
